Reuses a WebGPU drawable's bind groups while they bind the same resources.
Drawable::draw() released and recreated every bind group of every drawable on
every draw, wrote the drawable's UBO index on every draw, and built debug
strings it never used. Texture2D::setSamplerConfiguration() created a new
sampler on every call, and the atlas tweaker calls it each frame, so every
symbol's bind groups changed each frame too. A drawable now keeps each bind
group with the layout and entries it was built from, holding a reference on
each entry's buffer, sampler, and view so a handle it compares can't be reused
for another object, and rebuilds one only when they change. It writes the UBO
index only when it changes, and a sampler is kept when its state is unchanged.
With the patches after it, the browser demo builds about 22 bind groups a frame
while moving instead of 535.
Upstream: https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native/pull/4938

